    "query": "online programs that have low tuition",
    "response": "**Free or Low-Cost Online Programs**\n\n**Coursera:**\n* Coursera offers a wide range of free and low-cost courses from top universities and organizations.\n\n**edX:**\n* Similar to Coursera, edX provides free and affordable online courses from top institutions.\n\n**Google Digital Garage:**\n* Free online courses on digital marketing, data analytics, and other tech skills.\n\n**Khan Academy:**\n* A non-profit educational platform offering free online courses in math, science, computer science, and more.\n\n**MIT OpenCourseWare (OCW):**\n* Free access to course materials from Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT).\n\n**University of California, Berkeley Extension:**\n* Online certificate programs starting at $1,000-$2,000.\n\n**University of Maryland Global Campus:**\n* Undergraduate and graduate degrees with affordable tuition rates.\n\n**Western Governors University (WGU):**\n* Competency-based online university with low tuition fees.\n\n**Sophia Learning:**\n* Free and low-cost online courses that can transfer to accredited degree programs.\n\n**StraighterLine:**\n* Affordable online courses that can also transfer to degree programs.\n\n**Southern New Hampshire University (SNHU):**\n* Online programs with low tuition rates and financial aid options.\n\n**Other Low-Cost Online Programs:**\n\n**American Public University System:**\n* Affordable online degrees in various fields.\n\n**Colorado State University Global:**\n* Online programs with competitive tuition rates.\n\n**Grand Canyon University:**\n* Low-cost online degrees in a variety of areas.\n\n**Liberty University:**\n* Affordable online degrees with Christian values.\n\n**Note:** Tuition rates may vary depending on the program, university, and financial aid eligibility. It's recommended to research and compare different programs to find the best fit for your needs and budget.",
